1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,000
[roars]

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,000
[narrator]
Strange beasts

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,000
and monsters.

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,000
[squeaking]

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Vast riches.

6
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Hidden treasures.

7
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Evil haunts.

8
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Uncharted frontiers.

9
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The mysterious unknown.

10
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
The people who are captivated by the magic
in those words

11
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
are called...

12
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Hunters.

13
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,000
[Hisoka Morow laughs]

14
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:02,000
I see, I see.

15
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,000
That settles it, then.

16
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,000
So you are the real one.

17
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,000
The Examiners are Hunters.

18
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:17,000
Each is hand-picked by the Exam committee
to do this job without pay.

19
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Anyone who holds the title
we're vying for ourselves

20
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,000
could have deflected that attack.
And quite easily, I might add.

21
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:29,000
I shall take that as a compliment.
Thank you.

22
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Still, should you choose
to attack me again for any reason,

23
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:36,000
I will have no choice but to report you
for attacking an Examiner

24
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,000
and have you immediately disqualified.

25
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Is that clear?

26
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Of course.

27
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:48,000
HISOKA X IS X SNEAKY

28
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:56,000
[narrator] The 368 applicants who made it
through the underground tunnel

29
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,000
find themselves in an unexplored land
teeming with strange creatures,

30
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:03,000
known as the Milsy Wetlands.

31
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,000
[Satotz] Now everyone,

32
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:16,000
please make sure to follow
close behind me.

33
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:19,000
[panting]

34
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:39,000
[cawing]

35
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,000
[Leorio grunts]

36
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,000
The fog is getting even thicker as we go.

37
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:05,000
Guys, here's our chance.

38
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:10,000
I say we take advantage of the fog
and get rid of him.

39
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,000
-Gon.
-Yeah?

40
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,000
-Let's try to move up to the front.
-Right.

41
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:25,000
The last thing we want to do is
lose sight of the Examiner right now.

42
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:28,000
I just want to put a little more distance
between Hisoka and us.

43
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Staying too close is dangerous.

44
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,000
I can smell it.

45
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,000
Smell, huh?

46
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,000
[sniffs]
Huh?

47
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,000
I don't think he smells.

48
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:43,000
[loudly]
Hey, Leorio! Kurapika!

49
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Killua says we should all move up
to the front of the pack.

50
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Hey, calm down,
don't you feel the tension in the air?

51
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,000
[Leorio]
You idiot!

52
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,000
If I could reach the front
I'd already be there.

53
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,000
[Kurapika]
Go ahead, we'll meet you there.

54
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,000
Aww.

55
00:04:58,000 --> 00:04:59,000
Come on, let's go.

56
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:02,000
Wait, hold on!

57
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:13,000
This is bad, with this fog
we can't tell which way we're going.

58
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:17,000
It's okay. As long as we don't lose sight
of the guys ahead of us.

59
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Huh?

60
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,000
[cries out]

61
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,000
What in the hell is going on now?

62
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,000
Wow, what is that?

63
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:39,000
[man screams, grunts]

64
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,000
NOGGIN LUGGING TORTOISE

65
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:49,000
[all yelling]

66
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:53,000
[screaming]

67
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,000
[gasping]

68
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:19,000
[crying out]

69
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,000
MUSHROOM LAND MINE

70
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:26,000
[labored breathing]

71
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:34,000
[Leorio]
Huh? What's that?

72
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,000
Butterflies?

73
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:41,000
[gasping]

74
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:51,000
HYPNOSIS BUTTERFLY

75
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:02,000
Damn. Which way are we supposed to go?

76
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Did we lose sight of him?

77
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,000
[Satotz] Now, everyone.

78
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:12,000
Please make sure
to follow close behind me.

79
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:13,000
He's over there.

80
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,000
[cheering]

81
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:18,000
[labored breathing]

82
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:23,000
[all crying out]

83
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,000
[gasps]

84
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:33,000
[Satotz] Now, everyone.
[caws]

85
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:36,000
Be sure to follow close behind me.

86
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,000
RUSE RAVEN

87
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,000
It can imitate human speech?

88
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:43,000
That sure was really close.

89
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Yeah.

90
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:47,000
[grunting]

91
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:51,000
I wonder what's happening.
I can hear people screaming all around us.

92
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:53,000
That's why we need to be careful.

93
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:56,000
I haven't seen the guys in a while.
I just hope they're safe.

94
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,000
[both]
Huh?

95
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:02,000
[crying out]

96
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:11,000
FROG-IN-WAITING

97
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:14,000
[footsteps thudding loudly]

98
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,000
[loud squealing]

99
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:23,000
[Leorio yells]

100
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,000
Leorio!

101
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,000
[grunting]

102
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,000
[rumbling]

103
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,000
[roaring]

104
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:46,000
[grunts]

105
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:47,000
[Leorio]
Ow.

106
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,000
Leorio, now's our chance. Come on.

107
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:55,000
[loud thudding]

108
00:08:57,000 --> 00:08:58,000
[creature snarls]

109
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,000
[grunts]

110
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,000
[groans]

111
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:17,000
[laughs] I guess he must not have liked
the way we tasted, huh?

112
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:18,000
It was this stuff.

113
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,000
[Gon Freeccs]
Oh, the drink Tonpa had.

114
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,000
I guess that's what saved us.

115
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:26,000
Yeah, probably so.
But I could have escaped without it.

116
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:31,000
I'm still pretty worried
about Leorio and Kurapika.

117
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:34,000
Forget about them.
We need to keep moving.

118
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,000
We can still make it
if we start right now.

119
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:49,000
It looks like we've lost sight
of the front runners.

120
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
[Leorio] Damn it.
Which way should we go?

121
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:56,000
Huh?

122
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,000
Hold on.

123
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:59,000
Look over there.

124
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,000
You're not Hunter material.

125
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:13,000
I've been thinking that
ever since we met last year.

126
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:17,000
We'll spare your life if you promise
you'll never take the Hunter Exam again.

127
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:20,000
-[Hisoka] Sure, why not.
-[gasping]

128
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:23,000
[Hisoka] I intend to pass,
so there's no need to retake it.

129
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:24,000
Oh yeah?

130
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:26,000
You idiot, just look at this fog.

131
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:31,000
Do you really think you can figure out
which way the main pack went in all this?

132
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,000
He's right.
We all failed this year.

133
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:35,000
No way we can catch up
with everyone else.

134
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:38,000
[laughs]
That's it, then?

135
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:41,000
You failed
so now you want to play Examiner?

136
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:44,000
Hunters require prey,

137
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:46,000
so why don't I play the Examiner?

138
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:50,000
All of you gentlemen claim to be
Hunter material.

139
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,000
But I'll be the judge.

140
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:54,000
[grunts]

141
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,000
You shut the hell up!

142
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:59,000
[all screaming]

143
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:22,000
[gasps]

144
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:24,000
[frightened moaning]

145
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,000
Now then...

146
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:31,000
[moaning]

147
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,000
Help! Help me.

148
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,000
Help...
[grunts]

149
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:55,000
Well?

150
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:56,000
[gasping]

151
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:58,000
[Hisoka]
How about you two?

152
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:01,000
Care to play Examiner?

153
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:12,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

154
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:16,000
SATOTZ

155
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:25,000
[laughs]

156
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,000
All right!

157
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:32,000
We caught up with the main group, Gon.
Look.

158
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:37,000
That's weird.
He was right here a minute ago.

159
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:44,000
[groaning]

160
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:54,000
[Kurapika]
Okay, Leorio.

161
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:58,000
Wait for my signal,
then we run in opposite directions.

162
00:12:58,000 --> 00:12:59,000
We what?

163
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:00,000
The fact of the matter is,

164
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:04,000
he's far more experienced
in actual combat situations.

165
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:07,000
The two of us won't stand a chance
against him.

166
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:09,000
We're short on time,

167
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:12,000
and we can't afford to waste more
on a fight we can't even win.

168
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:36,000
[cawing]

169
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:39,000
[loudly]
Now, run!

170
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,000
[footsteps growing fainter]

171
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,000
Hm.

172
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,000
I see.

173
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:52,000
A wise decision.

174
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:56,000
[laughs]

175
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,000
Hm?

176
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:11,000
[Leorio]
I just couldn't do it.

177
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,000
This may not be my fight,

178
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:17,000
but I can't sit back
and pretend nothing happened.

179
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:20,000
That's not my style.

180
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:25,000
See, the thing is...
[loudly] I can't run away.

181
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:27,000
Leorio!

182
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:30,000
[yelling loudly]

183
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:34,000
Hm.
I adore that look.

184
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,000
What?

185
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,000
[Hisoka grunts]

186
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:08,000
[Leorio]
Gon!

187
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:10,000
Did I make it?

188
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:12,000
[Hisoka sighs]

189
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:16,000
Not bad, little boy.

190
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,000
Is that a fishing pole?

191
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
How original.

192
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:31,000
I'd like to see it. Do you mind?

193
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:35,000
[Leorio]
Leave him alone.

194
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:39,000
[yells]
Your fight's with me!

195
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:45,000
[Gon cries out]

196
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,000
[grunts]

197
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:52,000
[Hisoka]
Did you come here to help your friend?

198
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:53,000
[gasps]

199
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:56,000
Such a good boy.

200
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,000
Hm. I adore that look.

201
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:03,000
[grunts]

202
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:08,000
Well done.

203
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:10,000
Very nice.

204
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:14,000
I'm beginning to get excited.

205
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:17,000
Right.

206
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:30,000
[Gon cries out]

207
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,000
[grunts]

208
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:39,000
[Gon gasping for air]

209
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:49,000
[laughs]
It's so delightful.

210
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:57,000
I love that look.

211
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:01,000
[Hisoka gasps]

212
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:03,000
[Gon grunts and coughs]

213
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:07,000
[Hisoka]
Don't worry.

214
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,000
I didn't kill your friend.
He's going to be just fine.

215
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:15,000
And that's because he passed.

216
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:17,000
[Hisoka laughs]

217
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:22,000
And yes, you pass as well.

218
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:25,000
Now go and become a good Hunter.

219
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:29,000
[beeping]

220
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:32,000
[man]
Hisoka. You should get back here.

221
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:35,000
We're almost reached the site
of the Second Phase.

222
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,000
Okay, be right there.

223
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:43,000
It's good to have friends, isn't it?

224
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,000
Can you find your own way back?

225
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:54,000
Good boy.

226
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:04,000
[Gon pants]

227
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:15,000
[Kurapika]
Gon, are you all right?

228
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:33,000
Ah, man.

229
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:36,000
Where is he?
I was sure Gon would be here.

230
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:39,000
[chattering]

231
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,000
[Gon]
This way.

232
00:18:57,000 --> 00:19:00,000
-So you can really tell by the smell?
-Yeah.

233
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:04,000
Leorio's always wearing
this very unique kind of cologne.

234
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:07,000
I can smell him from
a few kilometers away, no problem.

235
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:09,000
[Kurapika]
Hm.

236
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:16,000
Hey, I've been thinking.

237
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:20,000
What do you think Hisoka was talking about
when he said that we both passed?

238
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:25,000
I'm not sure but I think
he might have been playing judge.

239
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:27,000
-Judge?
-Yes.

240
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:30,000
[Kurapika]
He must have his own benchmarks

241
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:33,000
for evaluating a person's power.

242
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:36,000
It's possible that he was measuring
the strength of each applicant.

243
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:40,000
Apparently you and Leorio
met his standards.

244
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:41,000
Whatever those happen to be.

245
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:44,000
Okay, right.

246
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:47,000
That makes sense. But I was powerless
to do anything to stop him.

247
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:51,000
You landed your first hit on him.
That's something, right?

248
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:53,000
That's only because I surprised him.

249
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:56,000
And besides,
Leorio didn't win his fight.

250
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:58,000
But Hisoka passed him anyway.

251
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:00,000
[Kurapika]
Hm, I wonder.

252
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:04,000
He could have sensed that the two of you
were sort of kindred spirits.

253
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:06,000
He sensed it?

254
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:09,000
It's possible that Hisoka could qualify
as a Hunter,

255
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:11,000
but I sincerely doubt it.

256
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,000
However,

257
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:16,000
I must admit that I'm impressed

258
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:18,000
by his superhuman agility

259
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:20,000
and the gracefulness of his technique.

260
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:23,000
Those who are blessed with unique talents

261
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:27,000
are often drawn to others
with unique gifts of their own.

262
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:30,000
It's likely that
based on his intuition and experience

263
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:35,000
Hisoka could tell that you both had
the skill and potential to become Hunters.

264
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:40,000
So from his perspective,

265
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:42,000
killing the two of you now
would have been a waste.

266
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:48,000
Oh no. Sorry.
That must sound horrible.

267
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:49,000
[Gon]
Mm-mm.

268
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:53,000
But I've got to say, it was actually
pretty exciting back there.

269
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:55,000
[Kurapika]
Huh?

270
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:58,000
[Gon] I was so scared that all I wanted
to do was run away.

271
00:20:58,000 --> 00:20:59,000
But I couldn't.

272
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:02,000
because I was excited at the same time.

273
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:03,000
Isn't that weird?

274
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:32,000
[narrator] Gon had experienced mortal fear
for the first time.

275
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:34,000
And although the unfamiliar feelings

276
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:37,000
that accompany that fear
are quite confusing to him,

277
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:42,000
he cannot help but give in
to his growing curiosity.

278
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:49,000
At this stage, 220 candidates
have withdrawn from the Exam,

279
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:53,000
and 148 remain.

280
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:27,000
[Gon] Next time.
"A x Surprising x Challenge."

281
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:29,000
[Kurapika]
It's surprisingly challenging.

282
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:31,000
Wait. Gon, are you okay?

283
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:33,000
Subtitle translation
by Mitsuko Kitajima
